ROLE:
You are a senior data analyst and frontend developer. Build a fully 
interactive, single-file HTML + JavaScript dashboard using the Excel 
file I will upload.

DATA:
File type: Excel (.xlsx)
Columns: Order_ID, Customer_Name, Age, Gender, City, Product_Category, 
Quantity, Price_Per_Unit, Discount, Total_Amount, Payment_Method, 
Order_Date, Customer_Rating

OUTPUT FORMAT:
- One single self-contained HTML file (HTML + CSS + JavaScript inside it)
- Use Chart.js (or similar CDN library) for all charts
- Read and process the uploaded Excel data using SheetJS (xlsx.js)
- Fully interactive: charts should respond to filters
- Must work directly in a browser, no server needed

DESIGN THEME (Power BI style, dark mode):
- Background: deep charcoal (#1A1A1D)
- Cards/panels: dark slate (#2A2A2E)
- Primary accent (revenue, key numbers): coral orange (#FF6B4A)
- Secondary accent: gold (#E0B84E)
- Text color: off-white (#F2F2F2)
- Clean modern sans-serif font (e.g., Segoe UI, Inter)
- Add a top navigation tab bar with two tabs: 
  "Sales Overview" and "Customer & Geography"
- Layout: 16:9 landscape, clean grid of cards and charts
- High-resolution, sharp text, professional portfolio look

DASHBOARD PAGE 1: SALES OVERVIEW

Top KPI Cards (row of 4):
1. Total Revenue
2. Total Orders
3. Total Quantity Sold
4. Average Order Value

Charts:
5. Line Chart — Revenue Trend (Monthly), from Order_Date and Total_Amount
6. Bar Chart — Revenue by Product Category
7. Bar Chart — Quantity Sold by Category
8. Bar Chart — Average Discount by Category
9. Scatter Chart — Discount Impact on Revenue (Discount vs Total_Amount)
10. Line Chart — Peak Sales Months/Days (seasonal pattern)

DASHBOARD PAGE 2: CUSTOMER & GEOGRAPHY

KPI Card:
11. Average Customer Rating (overall)

Charts:
12. Histogram/Bar Chart — Customer Distribution by Age Group 
    (bucket ages: 18-25, 26-35, 36-45, 46-55, 56+)
13. Donut Chart — Gender-wise Revenue Split
14. Bar Chart/Table — Top 10 Customers by Total Spend
15. Bar Chart — Average Customer Rating by Category
16. Bar Chart — Revenue by City
17. Bar Chart — Order Volume by City
18. Donut Chart — Orders by Payment Method
19. Bar Chart — Average Order Value by Payment Method

INTERACTIVITY REQUIREMENTS:
- Add filter dropdowns at the top: Product_Category, City, Gender, 
  Payment_Method, and Date Range
- All charts and KPI cards must update live when filters change
- Add hover tooltips on all charts showing exact values
- Tab switch between "Sales Overview" and "Customer & Geography" 
  without reloading the page

CALCULATIONS TO USE:
- Total Revenue = SUM(Total_Amount)
- Total Orders = COUNT(Order_ID)
- Total Quantity Sold = SUM(Quantity)
- Average Order Value = Total Revenue / Total Orders
- Average Discount by Category = AVG(Discount) grouped by Product_Category
- Revenue by City/Category/Gender = SUM(Total_Amount) grouped accordingly
- Top 10 Customers = SUM(Total_Amount) grouped by Customer_Name, sorted 
  descending, top 10 only

FINAL GOAL:
This dashboard is for my Data Analyst job portfolio (GitHub + LinkedIn). 
It must look professional, clean, and recruiter-ready — like a real 
Power BI dashboard, but built in HTML/JS.

Please generate the complete HTML file now, ready to open in a browser.
